  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 316 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nMedium range guidance shows a somewhat blocky pattern with a ridge \nover the Desert Southwest, another ridge in the western Atlantic, \nand a long wave trough sitting over the Midwest and Mississippi \nValley in between.  The pattern tries to become more progressive and \nzonal late in the weekend, but there aren't any obvious broad-scale \nforcing mechanisms to move the surface front.  In this case, the \nposition of the effective front will probably be determined by \noutflow from convection along it.  Temperatures will therefore be \ndifficult to forecast for Thursday into the weekend.  Current \nindications are that Thursday and Friday will be relatively cool in \nthe low to mid 80s with clouds and intermittent showers and a few \nthunderstorms.  However the 75th percentile of high temperatures \nfrom the LREF is just under 90 degrees, which is certainly possible \nif the front is farther north than expected.  The Bermuda High tries \nto build back to the west into the gulf and the southern U.S. late \nFriday into Saturday which would tend to bring southerly flow back \nto the Mid Mississippi Valley, and push the surface front north away \nfrom our area.  This will bring temperatures back into the upper 80s \nto low and mid 90s by Sunday/Monday.  The prevailing southerly flow \nwill also bring higher humidity back to the Mid Mississippi Valley \nand a threat for heat index values above 100 degrees.",
